      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Basilica of the National Shrine of Our Lady of San Juan del Valle, one of South Texas's largest churches, anchors the city’s historic center.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/San_Juan%2C_Texas",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Founded in 1909, San Juan grew around the railroad and the efforts of John Closner, who helped organize the community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/San_Juan%2C_Texas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The city borders Pharr to the west and Alamo to the east, with unincorporated Lopezville, Murillo, and North Alamo nearby.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/San_Juan%2C_Texas",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "San Juan’s post office, operated by the U.S. Postal Service, serves as a local hub for residents and visitors alike.",
